# Implementation Plan — Sprint-003B: Browser UI

Implement the **Browser Panel UI** (`src/ui/browser_panel.py`), encapsulating PySide6 `QWebEngineView` within a single-tab browser interface connected to `BrowserService`.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Scope is strictly limited to a single-tab browser view with Address Bar, Back/Forward/Refresh/Stop controls, SSL Security Indicator, Progress Bar, Error Handling, and Keyboard Shortcuts. Advanced features (multi-tab, bookmarks, downloads UI, DevTools) are excluded per sprint requirements.

> [!NOTE]
> All existing 47 automated tests will continue passing. UI unit tests for `BrowserPanel` will be added.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Presentation Layer (`src/ui/browser_panel.py`)

#### [NEW] [src/ui/browser_panel.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/browser_panel.py)
- `BrowserPanel`: Main browser panel component containing:
  - **Navigation Bar**: Back button, Forward button, Refresh/Stop button, SSL Lock Security Badge, Address Bar (`QLineEdit`), and Go button.
  - **Loading Progress Bar**: `QProgressBar` displayed beneath toolbar while `QWebEngineView` is loading content (0-100%).
  - **Web View Engine**: `QWebEngineView` rendering full web pages.
  - **Address Bar Integration**: Text editing normalization using `BrowserService.normalize_url()`. Typing a search query or domain triggers URL normalization.
  - **SSL Security Badge**: Updates icon/color based on HTTPS security (`https://` $\rightarrow$ Green Lock, `http://` $\rightarrow$ Orange Warning).
  - **Error Page Rendering**: Custom HTML error page displayed when `QWebEngineView.loadFinished(False)` fires, featuring URL details and a "Retry" button.
  - **Keyboard Shortcuts**: `Ctrl+L` (Focus address bar), `F5` / `Ctrl+R` (Reload), `Alt+Left` (Back), `Alt+Right` (Forward), `Esc` (Stop loading).

#### [MODIFY] [src/ui/main_window.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/main_window.py) & [src/app.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/app.py)
- Wire `BrowserPanel` into `MainWindow` panel stack (`PanelName.BROWSER`) passing `browser_service`.

#### [MODIFY] [src/ui/__init__.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/__init__.py)
